# Component File Anatomy

**Impact: MEDIUM-HIGH**

This rule applies to hand-written application components. It does not override framework-required files, generated code, tests, or vendor/shadcn primitive conventions.

## Standard component shape

1. **One exported application component per file.**
2. Components use an arrow function by project convention.
3. Props use a named `type` declared immediately above the component.
4. The application component is default-exported unless the framework/library context requires another export shape.
5. Reusable feature/shared components live in a PascalCase folder with a matching PascalCase file.
6. Component files SHOULD export the component only. Shared constants/styles/types/hooks belong in their owned colocated files.

```tsx
// PointsBreakdown/PointsBreakdown.tsx

type PointsBreakdownProps = {
  className?: string;
};

const PointsBreakdown = ({ className }: PointsBreakdownProps) => {
  return <div className={cn("flex flex-col gap-4", className)} />;
};

export default PointsBreakdown;
```

## Props

Application components with props SHOULD use a named prop type. Do not use an inline object type in the function signature merely because the component currently has one or two props.

The prop type stays in the component file when only that component consumes it. Extract to `ComponentName.types.ts` (or a domain-owned types file) only when multiple files need the same type.

Prefer `ComponentNameProps` when the generic name `Props` would be ambiguous in the surrounding file/tooling context.

## File exports

Do not turn component files into mini barrels/utilities.

Instead of:

```tsx
export const pillClass = "...";
export const getLabel = () => "...";
const PointsPill = () => null;
export default PointsPill;
```

use ownership-based colocated files when those values are shared:

```text
PointsPill/
  PointsPill.tsx
  PointsPill.constants.ts
```

A tiny private helper used only inside the component MAY stay in the file if it is not itself a component/public contract and extraction would reduce clarity.

## Folders

Feature/shared reusable components use:

```text
ComponentName/
  ComponentName.tsx
  ComponentName.constants.ts   # only if needed
  ComponentName.types.ts       # only if shared by multiple files
  __tests__/                   # when tests are warranted
```

Do not create empty companion files "for consistency".

Route/framework files (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, etc.) follow framework naming rather than PascalCase-folder rules.
